{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}bindsight — RNA-seq to de novo binder design{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>bindsight</h1>
<p class="lede">
  An open-source pipeline that joins cohort RNA-seq target discovery to de novo
  protein binder design in one reproducible workflow, with machine-readable
  provenance from every ranked binder back to the patient samples it came from.
</p>

<p class="prose">
  Genomics tooling stops at <em>“here are the interesting genes.”</em>
  Protein-design tooling starts at <em>“given a target…”</em>. The bridge between
  them is built ad-hoc, per project, and rarely reproducibly. bindsight ships
  that bridge as one tool and carries an audit trail across the join.
</p>

<div class="btn-row">
  <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/evidence">See what it has shown</a>
  <a class="btn" href="/try">Run the demo</a>
  <a class="btn" href="/your-data">Use your own data</a>
</div>

<h2>What it has, and has not, shown</h2>
<p class="prose muted">
  Stated here rather than further in, because the parts that did not work are
  the reason to trust the parts that did.
</p>

{% if not have_evidence %}
  <div class="note note--warn">
    <span class="note__glyph" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
    <div class="note__body">
      <p><strong>The evidence is not available in this install.</strong></p>
      <p class="small">
        <code>benchmarks/</code> ships with the repository, not the wheel. Clone
        the repository to see the study, the controls and the binders, or read
        them on <a href="{{ github }}/tree/main/benchmarks">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% else %}

<div class="grid grid--2">
  <section class="card">
    <h3 class="card__title">Discovery — one result survived its controls</h3>
    {% if study %}
      {% set gap = study.indication_gap %}
      {% if gap.get('point') is not none %}
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat__label">Indication-specific gap</span>
          <span class="stat__value">{{ fmt(gap.point, 3) }}</span>
          <span class="stat__ci">{{ interval(gap.low, gap.high, confidence=gap.get('confidence')) }}
            over {{ gap.get('n_clusters', ABSENT) }} antigens — excludes zero</span>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:.75rem">
          Known antigens rank higher in the cancer they are actually used in than
          in cancers that are not theirs. This is a claim about the ordering, not
          about any individual hit.
        </p>
      {% endif %}
      <p class="small">
        Against abundance-matched decoys the result is <strong>negative</strong>:
        {{ study.decoy_nominal }} of {{ study.decoy_rows|length }} pairs are
        nominally significant and
        <strong>{{ study.decoy_surviving_correction }}</strong> survive
        Benjamini-Hochberg.
      </p>
    {% endif %}
    <p><a href="/evidence">The study, its denominators and both nulls →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3 class="card__title">Design — the headline was withdrawn</h3>
    {% if designer %}
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat__label">Binders designed and folded</span>
        <span class="stat__value">{{ fmt_int(designer.n_designs) }}</span>
        <span class="stat__of">
          from {{ designer.n_trajectories or ABSENT }} backbones on
          {{ designer.gpu or 'a free GPU' }} — structures committed
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="withdrawn">
        <strong>success@0.65 is withdrawn as a measure of design quality.</strong>
        A paired control folded each design beside a shuffle of its own sequence;
        the shuffles cleared the bar more often than the designs did. The ipTM
        values are real Boltz-2 outputs — what does not follow is that the rate
        measures the designs.
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    <p><a href="/evidence#design">The control, and what it refuted →</a></p>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:1rem">
  <section class="card">
    <h3 class="card__title">Scope</h3>
    {% if study %}
      <div class="row">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat__label">Cohorts</span>
          <span class="stat__value">{{ study.n_projects }}</span>
          <span class="stat__of">whole, unstratified TCGA projects</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat__label">Antigen-cohort pairs</span>
          <span class="stat__value">{{ study.n_scored }}</span>
          <span class="stat__of">panel fixed in git before any cohort ran</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat__label">Surfaceome</span>
          <span class="stat__value">{{ fmt_int(study.surfaceome_size) }}</span>
          <span class="stat__of">eligible accessions</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3 class="card__title">What has not been done</h3>
    <ul class="small">
      <li>
        The three-way designer comparison against BindCraft and BoltzGen is
        <strong>not run</strong>: both need 24–32&nbsp;GB against anything larger
        than a small domain, so those arms require paid backends.
      </li>
      <li>
        The calibration's own power analysis puts <strong>142 paired designs</strong>
        at 80% power to detect a 0.05 ipTM difference. The committed control has 20.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Citing this</h2>
<p class="prose">{{ citation() }}</p>
{% endblock %}
